 :lesson/sections
 [{:section/type :communication-multiplied,
   :section/id 17,
   :section/title "Talking about you (all) in Spanish PART 2",
   :section/body
   ["You will remember from lesson 18 we made Spanish verbs plural by adding an N to the singular (second person) verb like this;"
    "you want you all want quiere quiereN you need you all need necesita necesitaN you can you all can puede puedeN It is just as easy to make these Synergy Verbs plural."
    "you are going to you (all) are going to va a vaN a you have to you all have to tiene que tieneN que"]}
  {:section/type :accuracy-pointer,
   :section/id 16,
   :section/title "Sí has two meanings",
   :section/body
   ["Look at the two words."
    "Yes = sí"
    "If = si"
    "Notice the accent over the letter í in sí - yes. That's the difference, it’s an emphasis on the letter í in sí - yes. Also, the context of conversation always tells whether sí means yes or si means if."]}],
 :lesson/number 19,
